+## 115. Old WordPress URLs land in one hop, 15 October
+
+Entry 93 claimed the `{/}?` sources sent an old URL to its new page in one hop. On production it
+was two: `trailingSlash: false` runs before the redirect list, so `/full-menu/` first 308ed to
+`/full-menu` and only then to `/menu`. Every old WordPress URL ends in a slash, so every indexed
+one was a chain. The versions without a slash were fine, which is why a spot check passed.
+
+`trailingSlash` is gone from `vercel.json`. A last redirect, `/:path+/` to `/:path+`, strips the
+slash from anything the specific rules did not match. Redirects are first match wins, so
+`/full-menu/` hits its own rule and goes straight to `/menu`, while `/menu/` still 308s to
+`/menu` and the canonicals are unchanged.
+
+Checked the order against path-to-regexp 6, the matcher Vercel uses: `/full-menu/` and
+`/full-menu` both to `/menu`, `/menu/` to `/menu`, `/menu`, `/`, `/sitemap.xml` and image paths
+untouched. Confirm on production after deploy with
+`curl -sIL https://www.senortequilas.com/full-menu/`, which should show one 308 then a 200.
+
+The apex adds one hop in front of all of this (`senortequilas.com` to www is a Vercel domain
+setting), so an old apex URL with a slash is two hops, down from three.
